name yardstick_150_high_jitter_40seeds
describe yardstick for #150: high_jitter with every v2 switch on, 40 seeds on both stacks (parity data only, no expectations)
# Not a regression test. `compare_seeds 40` makes sm_compare run 40 seeds so libwebrtc's per-seed spread is known:
# ours is bimodal (about a quarter of seeds never see an overuse in the first seconds and reach 53-65 % utilization).
compare_seeds 40
cc v2
pacer v2
tcc v2
rtx v2
rtcp v2
keyframe v2
allocator v2
packetization v2
audio v2
duration 30s
at 0s capacity=3000kbps delay=30ms jitter=40ms reorder=on queue=300ms
